\DOC induction_of

\TYPE {induction_of : hol_type -> thm}

\SYNOPSIS
The induction theorem of an inductive type.

\DESCRIBE
A call {induction_of ty} returns the induction theorem that was proved
when the type {ty} was defined, out of {inductive_type_store}; for {num}
it returns {num_INDUCTION}.

Where {ty} belongs to a family of types that were defined together, the
theorem is the one of the whole family: a predicate for each type of the
family, and a conclusion that is the conjunction of what each predicate
says. That is the theorem {INDUCT_FAMILY_TAC} uses;
{induction_for_type} cuts it down to the one type.

\FAILURE
Fails if {ty} is not a type that was defined by {define_type}, or {num}.

\EXAMPLE
{
  # induction_of `:(A)list`;;
  val it : thm =
    |- forall P.
           P [] /\ (forall a0 a1. P a1 ==> P (CONS a0 a1))
           ==> (forall x. P x)
}

\SEEALSO
cases_of, INDUCT_FAMILY_TAC, induction_for_type, induction_shape,
inductive_type_store, INDUCT_ON_TAC.

\ENDDOC
